Kind: ablation
Issue: #897
Takes out: the description dup() shares -- dup(), dup2() and dup3() give the new name a description of its own with the same libvfs fd, as a table of one description per descriptor would: closing the first name closes the file under the second, and musl_test's [30] must find the dup unable to seek once the first name is closed
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4
Expect: musl_test: \[30\] WRONG -- .*with [0-9]+ closed, [0-9]+ was at -1
Note: 4 of 4 caught and 4 of 4 passed at 0881d372 on OMEGA, TCG and KVM: with the first name closed, the dup's lseek() answered -1 in every ablated boot, where the fixed tree's answered 16; the same boots' [31] found the exec'd child's 20 and 21 at -1 as well, as dup2()'s names had descriptions of their own and the first close closed the file under them

